enchilada: CPU clocks: ask the big cluster for its top state once cpu4-7 are up (it stayed at 825 MHz)

Boot 5x (sweetcpufreq=1): "SWEET CPUFREQ: big enable 0x2 state 0 (825 MHz) of 27" and no "asked for"
line. SweetPlatformExpert::start() runs sweet_cpu_clocks() while SweetCPU is still bringing the
secondaries up (the lines interleave with cpu=3/cpu=4 CPU_ON): the big cluster is powered down, its
OSM reads enable bit 0 clear, and the request is skipped. Nothing asks again, so cpu4-7 ran at their
lowest state for the whole boot: a CPU-bound zsh loop (400k iterations) took 966-1009 ms whether run
alone or as 8 copies at once, i.e. the A75s at 825 MHz matched the A55s at 1766 MHz.

SweetCPU's start thread calls sweet_cpu_clocks() again after "N/N CPUs initialized". The function
is idempotent (only domains whose state differs from the best full-core row are written), so l3 and
little just log again; big should now log "asked for state 22 (2649 MHz), reads back 22". If it
still reads "enable 0x2", the OSM is not the one granting the big cluster's clock and the next step
is the LMh/EPSS registers, not a write here.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
@@ -157,6 +157,11 @@
  * always logs each domain's state and table (read only); boot-arg sweetcpufreq=1 asks for the
  * fastest state whose core count is the domain's full one (the rows with fewer cores are boost
  * states the hardware grants only to partly idle clusters), as Linux's cpufreq-hw does at "max".
+ *
+ * 0311: SweetCPU.cpp calls this again once every CPU is up. The first call runs while the big
+ * cluster (cpu4-7) is still powered down, and its OSM then reads "enable 0x2" (bit 0 clear), so it
+ * was left at state 0: boot 5x logged "big enable 0x2 state 0 (825 MHz)" and nothing after, and a
+ * CPU-bound loop took the same ~980 ms on every core, big or little.
  */
 #define OSM_ENABLE      0x000
 #define OSM_LUT         0x110
@@ -164,7 +169,8 @@
 #define OSM_LUT_ROWS    40
 #define OSM_PERF_STATE  0x920
 
-static void
+void sweet_cpu_clocks(void);     /* 0311: also SweetCPU.cpp */
+void
 sweet_cpu_clocks(void)
 {
 	static const struct {
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 
 extern "C" void sweet_secondary_entry(void);
 extern "C" boolean_t sweet_cpu_signal_is_enabled(unsigned int cpu);
+void sweet_cpu_clocks(void);     /* 0311: SweetPlatformExpert.cpp */
 
 class SweetCPU;
 static SweetCPU *sweet_cpus[MAX_CPUS];
@@ -191,6 +192,7 @@
 	IOLog("SWEET CPU: %u/%u CPUs initialized (%s)\n",
 	    topology->num_cpus, topology->num_cpus,
 	    smp != 0 ? "SGI1 verified" : "SMP disabled");
+	sweet_cpu_clocks();     /* 0311: again, now that the big cluster is powered (SweetPlatformExpert.cpp) */
 	thread_terminate(current_thread());
 }
 
